[
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:0.1", "PA_snp_5.1:0.2"], "en": "Sutta Nipāta 5.1 Vatthugāthā: In former times,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:1.1"], "en": "the cities of the Kosalans were delightful;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:1.2", "PA_snp_5.1:1.3", "PA_snp_5.1:1.4"], "en": "The brahmin, a master of the mantras, went to the southern region, longing for the state of nothingness.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:2.1"], "en": "Thus, in the territory of Assaka,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:2.2"], "en": "on the border of Aḷaka,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:2.3"], "en": "he dwelt on the bank of the Godhāvarī.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:2.4"], "en": "By means of gleaned grains and fruits,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:3.1", "PA_snp_5.1:3.2"], "en": "a vast village arose depending upon that very place.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:3.3"], "en": "Then, with the wealth produced from that,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:3.4", "PA_snp_5.1:4.1"], "en": "he prepared a great sacrifice. Having performed the great sacrifice, he—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:4.2"], "en": "He entered the hermitage again;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:4.3"], "en": "while he had just re-entered,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:4.4"], "en": "another brahmin arrived.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:5.1"], "en": "With swollen feet and parched,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:5.2", "PA_snp_5.1:5.3"], "en": "he approached him with mud-stained teeth and dust-covered hair.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:5.4"], "en": "He requested five hundred [disciples].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:6.1", "PA_snp_5.1:6.2"], "en": "Seeing him, Bāvarī invited him to take a seat.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:6.3", "PA_snp_5.1:6.4"], "en": "He inquired after his welfare and spoke these words:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:7.1"], "en": "\"Whatever gift I may have to give,\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:7.2"], "en": "“Everything has been given away by me;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:7.3"], "en": "give me your permission, Brahmā,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:7.4"], "en": "for I have no five hundred.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:8.1"], "en": "“If you do not grant my request,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:8.2", "PA_snp_5.1:8.3"], "en": "O Blessed One, on the seventh day from now, for you— ”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:8.4"], "en": "\"May his head split into seven pieces!", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:9.1"], "en": "Having thus prepared his deception,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:9.2"], "en": "the rogue uttered this terrifying threat.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:9.3"], "en": "Having heard those words of his,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:9.4"], "en": "Bāvarī became distressed;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:10.1"], "en": "he withered away, taking no food.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:10.2"], "en": "Afflicted by the dart of sorrow,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:10.3", "PA_snp_5.1:10.4"], "en": "his mind likewise finds no delight in jhāna.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:11.1"], "en": "Seeing him terrified and suffering,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:11.2", "PA_snp_5.1:11.3"], "en": "the deity who desired his welfare approached Bāvarī.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:11.4"], "en": "He spoke these words:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:12.1", "PA_snp_5.1:12.2"], "en": "“That deceiver, seeking wealth, does not understand the head.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:12.3", "PA_snp_5.1:12.4"], "en": "\"Whether on the head or at the fall of the head, no knowledge exists for him.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:13.1"], "en": "\"Lady, you indeed know; [tell me]...\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:13.2"], "en": "\"Tell me that when asked:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:13.3"], "en": "the head and the striking of the head.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:13.4"], "en": "We shall listen to your words.\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:14.1"], "en": "“I too do not know this;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:14.2", "PA_snp_5.1:14.3"], "en": "no knowledge exists here regarding the blow to the head and the one who struck the head.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:14.4"], "en": "For here is the vision of the Conquerors.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:15.1", "PA_snp_5.1:15.2"], "en": "But who indeed knows on this circle of the earth:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:15.3"], "en": "“The head and the striking of the head—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:15.4"], "en": "explain that to me, O deity.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:16.1"], "en": "“Formerly, from Kapilavatthu...”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:16.2"], "en": "The Leader of the World has gone forth;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:16.3"], "en": "the descendant of King Okkāka,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:16.4"], "en": "the Son of the Śākyas, the Radiant One.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:17.1"], "en": "For such, O Brahmin, is the Fully Awakened One:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:17.2"], "en": "one who has gone to the further shore of all phenomena,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:17.3"], "en": "having attained all higher knowledges and powers.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:17.4"], "en": "Possessing vision regarding all phenomena,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:17.5", "PA_snp_5.1:17.6"], "en": "he has attained the destruction of all karma and is liberated through the exhaustion of the substrata of existence.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:18.1"], "en": "He is the Buddha, the Blessed One, in the world;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:18.2"], "en": "he who possesses the eye teaches the Dhamma.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:18.3"], "en": "Go to him and ask him.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:18.4"], "en": "\"He will explain that to you.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:19.1", "PA_snp_5.1:19.2"], "en": "Having heard the words \"The Fully Awakened One,\" Bāvari was filled with joy.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:19.3"], "en": "Soka’s affliction was diminished,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:19.4"], "en": "and he attained abundant rapture.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:20.1"], "en": "Bāvari, being satisfied and uplifted, [spoke].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:20.2"], "en": "Born of wisdom, he questions that deity:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:20.3"], "en": "\"In which village or town,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:20.4"], "en": "or in which country, is the Lord of the World?\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:20.5", "PA_snp_5.1:20.6"], "en": "“Where we might go and see the Fully Enlightened One, the supreme among bipeds.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:21.1"], "en": "“In Sāvatthī, the city of the Kosalans, the Victor dwells;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:21.2"], "en": "Possessing abundant wisdom and excellent, vast intelligence,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:21.3"], "en": "that son of the Sakyas is steadfast and free from taints; he is the sage,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:21.4"], "en": "the bull among men, who knows how to endure even the falling of a thunderbolt upon his head.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:22.1"], "en": "Then he addressed his disciples,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:22.2"], "en": "the brahmins who had mastered the mantras:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:22.3"], "en": "\"Come, young men, I shall tell you...\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:22.4"], "en": "Listen to my words:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:23.1", "PA_snp_5.1:23.2"], "en": "he whose manifestation is so rare in the world, yet occurs so frequently.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:23.3", "PA_snp_5.1:23.4"], "en": "Today, the one renowned as the Fully Awakened One has appeared in this world;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:23.5"], "en": "having gone quickly to Sāvatthī, [he will teach].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:23.6"], "en": "“Go forth to see the Supreme among Bipeds.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:24.1"], "en": "“How indeed shall we know him as a Buddha,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:24.2"], "en": "O Brahmin, even after seeing him?”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:24.3"], "en": "\"Tell us who do not know,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:24.4"], "en": "so that we may understand it.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:25.1"], "en": "\"For they have come down in the mantras...\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:25.2", "PA_snp_5.1:25.3"], "en": "The thirty-two marks of a Great Man have been explained in their entirety,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:25.4"], "en": "in proper sequence.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:26.1", "PA_snp_5.1:26.2"], "en": "For one in whose limbs these marks of a Great Man exist,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:26.3"], "en": "there are only two possible destinies.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:26.4"], "en": "For a third [opportunity] does not exist.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:27.1"], "en": "If he dwells in a household,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:27.2"], "en": "he might conquer this earth.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:27.3"], "en": "Without punishment, without weapons,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:27.4", "PA_snp_5.1:28.1"], "en": "he instructs by means of the Dhamma. And if he goes forth into homelessness, [he does so] by means of the Dhamma.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:28.2"], "en": "From the household life to homelessness;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:28.3"], "en": "the Fully Awakened One, whose shelter is open,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:28.4"], "en": "becomes an unsurpassed Arhat.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:29.1"], "en": "Birth, clan, and characteristics,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:29.2"], "en": "mantras, and further,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:29.3"], "en": "disciples; the head, and the striking of the head—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:29.4"], "en": "Ask with your mind alone:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:30.1", "PA_snp_5.1:30.2"], "en": "\"If the Buddha will appear, he is one whose vision is unobstructed.\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:30.3", "PA_snp_5.1:30.4"], "en": "“The questions asked by mind he will answer with speech.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:31.1"], "en": "Having heard Bāvari’s words,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:31.2"], "en": "The disciples were sixteen brahmins:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:31.3"], "en": "Ajita, Tissa Metteyya,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:31.4"], "en": "Puṇṇaka, and then Mettagū.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:32.1"], "en": "Dhotaka and Upasīva,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:32.2", "PA_snp_5.1:32.3"], "en": "Nanda and Hemaka; both Todeyya and Kappa—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:32.4"], "en": "And the wise Jaṭukaṇṇī,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:33.1"], "en": "Bhadrāvudha, Udaya,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:33.2"], "en": "and the brahmin Posāla as well;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:33.3"], "en": "Mogharāja, the wise one,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:33.4"], "en": "and Piṅgiya, the great seer—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:34.1"], "en": "all these leaders of independent groups—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:34.2"], "en": "Renowned throughout the entire world,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:34.3"], "en": "these wise ones delight in meditation,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:34.4"], "en": "being perfumed by their former mental impressions.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:35.1", "PA_snp_5.1:35.2"], "en": "Having paid homage to Bāvarī and circumambulated him,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:35.3"], "en": "all those wearing matted hair and deerskins—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:35.4"], "en": "Setting out toward the north,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:36.1"], "en": "they reached the city of Alakassapātiṭṭhāna,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:36.2"], "en": "which was then called Purimāhissati.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:36.3"], "en": "Ujjenī and also Gonaddha,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:36.4"], "en": "Vedisa and that called Vanasa,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:37.1"], "en": "and also Kosambī and Sāketa.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:37.2"], "en": "And Sāvatthī, the supreme city;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:37.3"], "en": "Setavya, Kapilavatthu,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:37.4"], "en": "and Kusinārā, the sacred abode.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:38.1"], "en": "Pāvā and the city of Bhoga,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:38.2"], "en": "Vesālī and the Magadhan capital,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:38.3"], "en": "and the Pāsāṇaka Cetiya.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:38.4"], "en": "Delightful and heart-gladdening,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:39.1"], "en": "like a thirsty man finding cool water,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:39.2"], "en": "or a merchant gaining a great profit.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:39.3"], "en": "Like those oppressed by the heat,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:39.4"], "en": "they hurriedly climbed the mountain.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:40.1"], "en": "At that time, the Blessed One—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:40.2"], "en": "Honored by the community of bhikkhus,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:40.3"], "en": "he teaches the Dhamma to the bhikkhus,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:40.4"], "en": "roaring like a lion in the forest.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:41.1"], "en": "Ajita saw the Buddha,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:41.2"], "en": "like the sun with its hundred rays,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:41.3"], "en": "like the moon on the fifteenth day.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:41.4"], "en": "Having reached full perfection,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:42.1", "PA_snp_5.1:42.2"], "en": "he saw his limbs and his perfectly complete physical characteristics.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:42.3"], "en": "Standing to one side, joyful,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:42.4"], "en": "he asked about the questions on the mind:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:43.1"], "en": "\"Tell me of the origin of the world.\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:43.2"], "en": "Tell me of lineage and its characteristics;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:43.3"], "en": "tell me of mastery over the mantras;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:43.4"], "en": "and how many recitations does a brahmin perform?", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:44.1"], "en": "“His lifespan was one hundred and twenty years,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:44.2"], "en": "and he was Bāvari by clan;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:44.3"], "en": "there were three marks upon his body.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:44.4"], "en": "He had mastered the three Vedas,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:45.1"], "en": "as well as the science of marks (lakkhaṇa), the histories (itihāsa),", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:45.2"], "en": "and the lexicons (nighaṇḍu) along with their commentaries (keṭubha).", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:45.3"], "en": "He taught five hundred [disciples],", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:45.4"], "en": "having reached perfection in the True Dhamma.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:46.1"], "en": "[He taught] the investigation of the marks.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:46.2"], "en": "O Bāvari, best among men,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:46.3", "PA_snp_5.1:46.4"], "en": "O cutter of doubt, explain this so that we may have no lingering uncertainty.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:47.1"], "en": "The mouth covers the tongue;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:47.2"], "en": "there is wool between the eyebrows;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:47.3"], "en": "the private parts are enclosed in a sheath.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:47.4"], "en": "\"Know this thus, young man:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:48.1"], "en": "for one who does not hear any question at all,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:48.2"], "en": "yet hears the questions answered,\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:48.3", "PA_snp_5.1:48.4"], "en": "All the people, filled with wonder, reflected with palms joined:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:49.1"], "en": "\"Who indeed is this— whether a deva or a Brahmā?\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:49.2", "PA_snp_5.1:49.3"], "en": "Or even if Sujampati himself were asked these questions in his mind,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:49.4"], "en": "what would he be able to say in reply?", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:50.1", "PA_snp_5.1:50.2"], "en": "“Bāvari asks concerning the head and the striking of the head;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:50.3"], "en": "may the Blessed One explain that.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:50.4"], "en": "\"Dispel our doubt, O Sage.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:51.1"], "en": "\"Know that ignorance is the head's fetter;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:51.2"], "en": "wisdom is that which strikes down the head.\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:51.3"], "en": "“Endowed with faith, mindfulness, and concentration,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:51.4"], "en": "and joined with desire and energy,” then,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:52.1"], "en": "through great feeling,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:52.2", "PA_snp_5.1:52.3", "PA_snp_5.1:52.4"], "en": "Having steadied himself, the young man placed his deerskin mantle over one shoulder and prostrated with his head at [the Buddha's] feet.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:53.1"], "en": "“The brahmin Bāvarī,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:53.2"], "en": "together with his disciples, O dear sir,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:53.3"], "en": "is uplifted in heart and well-pleased.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:53.4"], "en": "“The Eyeful One pays homage at his feet.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:54.1", "PA_snp_5.1:54.2"], "en": "“May the brahmin Bāvarī be well, together with his disciples.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:54.3"], "en": "And may you also be happy;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:54.4"], "en": "live long, young man,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:55.1"], "en": "both for Bāvari and for yourself.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:55.2"], "en": "\"Ask whatever you desire;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:55.3"], "en": "all have been granted leave to ask,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:55.4"], "en": "so let all your doubts be resolved.\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:56.1"], "en": "Having been granted leave by the Fully Enlightened One,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:56.2", "PA_snp_5.1:56.3"], "en": "Ajita sat down with palms joined and asked his first question.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:56.4"], "en": "Therein he questioned the Tathāgata.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_snp_5.1:56.5"], "en": "The introductory verses are concluded.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:11:20Z"}
]
